[38;5;231m⏺[39m Holding off on the edit for one thing: [38;5;153mSESSION_TIMEOUT_MINUTES[39m is a session lifetime, so this is a security-posture
  change, not just a value swap. Going 30 → 480 means a stolen or abandoned session stays valid for 8 hours instead of
  30 minutes — an unattended browser, a shared machine, or a leaked session token all get a 16x wider window.
  [38;5;153mserver.js:2[39m confirms it's the actual session expiry, not a display value.

